%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5976006531153724f8306a1fd441aa0c, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dispatch_Ch3_Boss
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: RobotRescue.Runtime::RobotRescue.Narrative.DispatchScript
  lines:
  - cue: intro
    text: 'BIG RESCUE! Mittens the cat is up the old oak, and every hum scares her higher. Rosa''s ladder fell in the last tremor. Screw its brackets back on, climb up, and bring Mittens home to her basket. And PIP: hold on tight when it hums.'
    duration: 11
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: ladder_up
    text: Ladder's up! The bottom of the trunk is too smooth to climb, but the knobbly bark higher up is grippy. Climb past a branch, then jump off the trunk onto it.
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: cat_flee_1
    text: She ran higher! Cats. Honestly.
    duration: 3
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: cat_top
    text: She's on the very top branch now, and she's just realised she can't get down. Classic cat. Climb up the north side past her branch and jump across, or go right to the top and drop down.
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: cat_grabbed
    text: Got her! You can't climb with your hands full, so get down carefully. Cats land on their feet. You don't.
    duration: 6
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: throw
    text: Did you just THROW the cat? ...She landed on her feet. Rosa would like a word.
    duration: 5
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: cat_home
    text: Mittens is home! Purring and everything. Rosa's crying a little. Good tears.
    duration: 5
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: hum_tremor_first
    text: Hang on! THAT's the hum! Feel the oak shaking? It shakes the roots loose every time. It's coming from under the water.
    duration: 7
    repeatable: 0
  - cue: hum_tremor
    text: Here it comes again! Grip!
    duration: 2.5
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: hum_tremor
    text: Hum! Hold on to something!
    duration: 2.5
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: fell
    text: Ooh, long way down. Back to the bottom.
    duration: 3
    repeatable: 1
  - cue: exit
    text: Rescue complete! And PIP, the oak was shaking in time with the hum. Short short short, long long long. Whoever's sending it, they're getting weaker.
    duration: 8
    repeatable: 0
